      "content": "#include \"knn.h\"\n\nchar knn(int n_groups, Group * groups, int k, Point to_evaluate) {\n    float *heap_dist = (float *) malloc(sizeof(float) * k);\n    char *heap_label = (char *) malloc(sizeof(char) * k);\n    int hsize = 0;\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\n        Group g = groups[i];\n        float px = to_evaluate.x;\n        float py = to_evaluate.y;\n\n        for (int j = 0; j < g.length; j++) {\n            float dx = g.points[j].x - px;\n            float dy = g.points[j].y - py;\n            float d = dx * dx + dy * dy;\n\n            if (hsize < k) {\n                int pos = hsize++;\n                heap_dist[pos] = d;\n                heap_label[pos] = g.label;\n\n                while (pos > 0) {\n                    int parent = (pos - 1) >> 1;\n                    if (heap_dist[parent] < heap_dist[pos]) {\n                        float td = heap_dist[parent];\n                        heap_dist[parent] = heap_dist[pos];\n                        heap_dist[pos] = td;\n\n                        char tl = heap_label[parent];\n                        heap_label[parent] = heap_label[pos];\n                        heap_label[pos] = tl;\n\n                        pos = parent;\n                    } else {\n                        break;\n                    }\n                }\n            } else if (d < heap_dist[0]) {\n                heap_dist[0] = d;\n                heap_label[0] = g.label;\n\n                int pos = 0;\n                while (1) {\n                    int left = (pos << 1) + 1;\n                    int right = left + 1;\n                    int largest = pos;\n\n                    if (left < hsize && heap_dist[left] > heap_dist[largest]) {\n                        largest = left;\n                    }\n                    if (right < hsize && heap_dist[right] > heap_dist[largest]) {\n                        largest = right;\n                    }\n\n                    if (largest != pos) {\n                        float td = heap_dist[pos];\n                        heap_dist[pos] = heap_dist[largest];\n                        heap_dist[largest] = td;\n\n                        char tl = heap_label[pos];\n                        heap_label[pos] = heap_label[largest];\n                        heap_label[largest] = tl;\n\n                        pos = largest;\n                    } else {\n                        break;\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    int freq[256] = {0};\n    for (int i = 0; i < hsize; i++) {\n        freq[(unsigned char)heap_label[i]]++;\n    }\n\n    // The original implementation initializes all k slots with label -1.\n    // If fewer than k points were seen, those missing slots still participate\n    // in the frequency count and tie-breaking.\n    if (hsize < k) {\n        freq[255] += k - hsize;\n    }\n\n    char best = 0;\n    int best_count = -1;\n    for (int c = -128; c <= 127; c++) {\n        unsigned char idx = (unsigned char)c;\n        if (freq[idx] > best_count) {\n            best_count = freq[idx];\n            best = (char)c;\n        }\n    }\n\n    free(heap_dist);\n    free(heap_label);\n    return best;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n_groups = parse_number_of_groups();\n    \n    Group * groups = (Group *) malloc(sizeof(Group) * n_groups);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\n        groups[i] = parse_next_group();\n    }\n\n    int k = parse_k();\n\n    Point to_evaluate = parse_point();\n\n    printf(\"%c\", knn(n_groups, groups, k, to_evaluate));\n}\n",
      "path": "src/knn.c"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Replacing the O(N*k) insertion-sort selection with a binary max-heap of size k reduces asymptotic complexity to O(N log k), keeps only a small contiguous working set for better cache behavior, and avoids qsort overhead by counting label frequencies directly from heap contents.",
  "notes": "The heap stores squared distances (no sqrt needed). Tie-breaking matches the original: missing slots are counted as label -1, and among equal maximum frequencies the smallest signed char value wins. Only src/knn.c was modified; parsing and data layout remain unchanged to minimize risk.",
  "sources_kept": [],
